@startuml client-screens
!include style.iuml
title Client 1/2: screens and connection (package client)

class Main {
    .. the application: shows one screen at a time,\nowns the connection ..
    + showScreen(next)
    + connect(address) / startSolo(name)
    + play(map)
}

package "Screens, in order" #EEF4FF {
    class NameScreen {
        .. 1. nickname + server address ..
    }
    class LobbyScreen {
        .. 2. teams, brawler, map, start ..
    }
    class GameScreen {
        .. 3. the match (see diagram 2/2) ..
    }
}

class LobbyView <<final>> {
    .. decides what the lobby shows\n(plain Java, tested) ..
}

package "Connection: solo or network" #EEFBEF {
    interface GameSession {
        .. "a match I take part in" ..
        + join(name) / chooseTeam(team)
        + chooseBrawler(brawler)
        + chooseMap(map) / start()
    }
    class LocalSession {
        .. solo: server in the same program ..
    }
    class RemoteSession {
        .. network: KryoNet connection ..
    }
}

Main -down-> NameScreen : shows first
NameScreen -[#1E64C8,bold]right-> LobbyScreen : <color:#1E64C8>join accepted</color>
LobbyScreen -[#1E64C8,bold]right-> GameScreen : <color:#1E64C8>leader starts</color>
GameScreen -[#1E64C8,bold,dashed]up-> LobbyScreen : <color:#1E64C8>match finished</color>
LobbyScreen -down-> LobbyView : asks what to show

Main *-right- "0..1" GameSession : owns
LobbyScreen -down-> GameSession : join, team, brawler,\nmap, start
GameSession <|.down. LocalSession : implements
GameSession <|.down. RemoteSession : implements

$legend("<b>Inheritance</b>: Main extends libGDX Game; every screen extends ScreenAdapter.", "<b>Polymorphism</b>: screens use a GameSession without knowing if it is solo or network.", "<color:#1E64C8><b>Blue arrows</b></color>: the order of the screens.")
@enduml
